<Chapters>
	<Chapter>
		<Name>Keswick Reservoir</Name>
		<Region>Keswick</Region>
		<resolution>high</resolution>
		<Sections>
			<Section>
				<Header>Keswick Reservoir Temperatures</Header>
				<Object>
					<Type>textbox</Type>
					<Text>Temperature profiles plots represent the vertical distribution of water temperatures in the lake. Because water temperatures impact density, warmer waters occupy the surface portions of the lake and cooler waters occupy the deeper portions of the lake. In the winter or in shallower reservoirs with substantial flow through, vertical temperature profiles can be uniform from the surface to the bottom (Isothermal conditions). 

These plots compare simulated and observed temperature profiles throughout the calendar year that aided in model calibration.  Temperature (%%degrees%%F) is represented on the x-axis and elevation (ft) is represented on the y-axis.  Generally, observed temperature profiles were available monthly; however, in certain years profiles were more or less frequently.   When there are more than 12 observed temperature profiles available for a year, the information is presented in two graphs. If the lake has multiple locations observed profiles, individual graphs are provided for each location or at the site immediately upstream of the dam (not all locations are available in all years).

Each profile includes the date, observed (light blue) and simulated (red-dashed) water temperature profile, and observed (dark blue) and simulated (dark red dashed) water surface elevation (WSE) on the date of the simulation (plotted as a horizontal line at the respective elevation).
</Text>
				</Object>

				<Object>
					<Type>ProfilePlot</Type>
					<Description>Keswick Reservoir near dam temperature profiles, %%year%%. ResSim.</Description>
					<Template>format/templates/Plot_Defaults_KES_TW.xml</Template>
					<unitsystem>english</unitsystem>
					<XLabel>Temperature (%%units%%)</XLabel>
					<SplitByYear>True</SplitByYear>
					<Parameter>Temperature</Parameter>
					<profilesperrow>4</profilesperrow>
					<DatesSource>Observed_S1</DatesSource>
<!--					<XLims>
						<min>0</min>
						<max>30</max>
					</XLims>
					<YLims>
						<min>500</min>
						<max>590</max>
					</YLims>
					<xticks>
						<spacing>5</spacing>
					</xticks> -->
					<Lines>
						<Line>
							<label>Simulated</label>
							<Flag>Computed</Flag>
							<Parameter>Temperature</Parameter>
							<ResSimResName>Keswick Reservoir</ResSimResName>
							<lineColors>
								<linecolor>red</linecolor>
								<linecolor>green</linecolor>
								<linecolor>orange</linecolor>
							</lineColors>
							<lineStylePattern>dashed</lineStylePattern>
							<lineWidth>2</lineWidth>
							<zorder>4</zorder>
						</Line>
						<Line>
							<label>%%SimulationName%%</label>
							<Flag>Computed</Flag>
							<Parameter>Temperature</Parameter>
							<w2_segment>101</w2_segment>
							<linecolors>
								<linecolor>darkgreen</linecolor>
								<linecolor>maroon</linecolor>
								<linecolor>violet</linecolor>
							</linecolors>
							<lineStylePattern>dashed</lineStylePattern>
							<lineWidth>2</lineWidth>
							<zorder>4</zorder>
						</Line>
						<Line>
							<label>Observed R1</label>
							<Flag>Observed_S1</Flag>
							<Parameter>Temperature</Parameter>
							<lineColor>#5b9bd5</lineColor>
							<lineWidth>2</lineWidth>
							<zorder>4</zorder>
							<FileName>%%observedDir%%\Keswick_R1_2010_2017-2020.txt</FileName>
							<units>C</units>
						</Line>
					</Lines>
					<hlines>
						<hline>
							<flag>waterlevel</flag>
							<label>Simulated WSE</label>
							<parameter>elevation</parameter>
							<interval>1HOUR</interval>
							<Type>PER-AVER</Type>
							<DSS_Path>//Keswick Reservoir-Pool/Elev//1Hour/%%Fpart%%/</DSS_Path>
							<DSS_Filename>%%ModelDSS%%</DSS_Filename>
							<scalar>1</scalar>
							<linecolor>darkred</linecolor>
						</hline>
					</hlines>
				</Object>


